hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24290","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan: That al-Dahhak ibn Qays wrote to Qays ibn al-Haytham when Yazid ibn Mu'awiyah died: Peace be upon you; to proceed: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Before the Hour there will be tribulations like pieces of the dark night, and tribulations like pieces of smoke, in which the heart of a man dies as his body dies. A man wakes a believer and sleeps a disbeliever, and sleeps a believer and wakes a disbeliever. In them some people sell their share and their religion for a small price of this world. And Yazid ibn Mu'awiyah has died, and you are our brothers and our kin, so do not precede us in anything until we choose for ourselves."
